[step] The tab lock's two-stage bore — the 2 mm head counterbore reaches the pad/tongue root at X -98.65, while the 1.2 mm shaft bore stops at X -98.25 after clearance. Their 0.4 mm offset is the positive shoulder that seats the rigid lock head, not an unintended near-flush exterior step.
